Another method is to conduct a thorough code review, where you manually examine the code and its interactions with other components. This can be done by yourself or with the help of a peer reviewer. It's also essential to write comprehensive tests, including unit tests, integration tests, and end-to-end tests, to verify the functionality of the changed code and its impact on the overall system.

To further increase the reliability of your dependency spotting and testing, consider implementing a continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipeline. This will allow you to automatically run tests and verify the integrity of your codebase with each change, providing immediate feedback on potential issues.

